# UST.G3AP Selected Cayley Ordinary-Top Lower-Bound Theorem

Date: 2026-08-10

## Status

```text
CLOSED_EXACT_SELECTED_F1016_ORDINARY_TOP_DIMENSION_AT_LEAST_ONE
```

This theorem closes only the lower half of G3AP. It does not assert that the
ordinary top is one-dimensional or identify its generator.

## Statement

Let `Phi=uK+vE+sC` be the exact selected `F_101^6` Cayley member used in
G3AO, and let `J` be its ordinary partial-Jacobian ideal. Then

```text
dim_F1016 (S/J)_(18,2,2) >= 1.
```

## Proof

G3AO proves that the logarithmic critical locus of this same selected member
is empty on all 735 nonempty Cox support orbits. The common Cayley semigroup
ring is normal and therefore Cohen-Macaulay. Its eight logarithmic derivatives
form a homogeneous system of parameters and hence a regular sequence.

The tautological Cayley class is big and nef. Its top self-intersection is

```text
14301 = 60 mod 101,
```

which is a unit in the selected residue field. Toric residue duality for the
regular logarithmic sequence therefore gives a nonzero `R1` top residue in

```text
8 beta - 2 beta0 = (18,2,2).
```

Let `P` denote the Cox coordinate product. For every ordinary derivative,

```text
P partial_i(Phi) = (P/x_i) (x_i partial_i(Phi)).
```

Thus the ordinary Jacobian quotient maps onto the logarithmic/saturated `R1`
quotient in the top degree. Since the selected `R1` top is nonzero, the
ordinary top quotient has dimension at least one.

## Consequence

To finish G3AP it is now enough to prove an upper bound of one. A candidate
list of exact selected-module elements suffices if:

1. every candidate element belongs to the selected module;
2. all 21 original quotient-module generators divide to zero by that list;
3. the monomial module generated by the candidate leading terms leaves at
   most one of the 174,865 target monomials.

The list need not be certified as an unrestricted Groebner basis. Its leading
monomial module is contained in the true initial module, so condition 3 gives
an upper bound. This theorem supplies the matching lower bound.

## Guardrails

This theorem does not close the exact dimension, response ranks,
characteristic-zero promotion, `beta_C`, or the physical Hull-Strominger
endpoint.

